                                <br />
                            </h5>
                            <br />

                            <div class="mb-3">
                                Data science courses are open to a wide range of individuals, from students fresh out of high school to working professionals looking to switch careers. While a background in STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics) is traditionally preferred, modern programs and certifications are designed to accommodate diverse academic backgrounds.

                            </div>
                            <div   class="mb-3">
                                <ul>
                                    <li>
                                            <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>  <b>Science Stream</b> :
                                        <div style="margin-left:2%" class="mb-3">
                                            Students with Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics (PCM) are most eligible for technical degrees like B.Tech in Data Science.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                            <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i> <b>Commerce/Arts Streams</b> :
                                        <div style="margin-left:2%" class="mb-3">
                                            Students from these backgrounds can pursue BCA (Data Science) or B.Sc. programs that focus on application rather than pure engineering.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                            <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>  <b>Key Requirements</b> :
                                        <div style="margin-left:2%" class="mb-3">
                                            Most universities require a minimum of 50–60% aggregate marks in the 12th board exams.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                            <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>   <b>Relevant Degrees</b> :
                                        <div style="margin-left:2%" class="mb-3">
